{"base_rate":0.33663366336633666,"brier":0.17315275813295614,"bss":0.22461313181989218,"bss_hi":0.31330523665085885,"bss_lo":0.1438863288883426,"chart":{"base":[498.5,171.0],"fp":[296.5,251.1],"lead":"62,42.4 272,33.2 482,25.6 692,17.7","note":{"base":"skill 0.22 — higher than 22% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 3.1 °C — better than 0% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 5%; promised 91% → rained 70%"},"rel":"63.3,444 105.2,375.5 327,192.2 634.3,163.9"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13603960396039605,"ess":445.67554670804213,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Philadelphia</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Philadelphia rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>70%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 707 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPHILADELPHIA 3.6 SSW, 1.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.22, ranked 104 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(67&ndash;116) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>201</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>87</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Philadelphia</b> <span class=\"muted\">US</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.22</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>67&ndash;116\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>707 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Philadelphia &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Philadelphia\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" heigh